        "subject": "economics",
        "chapter": "National Income & Related Aggregates",
        "concept_id": "economics:product-method-double-counting",
        "body": "Farmers produce wheat worth ₹150. Bakers buy ₹60 of that wheat and use it to make bread worth ₹240; assume no other intermediate inputs. What total value is counted by the product method when intermediate value is not counted twice?",
        "options": [
          {
            "key": "A",
            "text": "₹330"
          },
          {
            "key": "B",
            "text": "₹390"
          },
          {
            "key": "C",
            "text": "₹240"
          },
          {
            "key": "D",
            "text": "₹150"
          }
        ],
        "correct_answer": "A",
        "explanation": "Count the farmers’ ₹150 output and the bakers’ value added of ₹240 − ₹60 = ₹180. Total value added is ₹330.",
        "route": "conceptual",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "question_type": "conceptual_mcq",
        "passage_text": null,
